<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commentātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		2. commentor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An inventor</i>, <i>contriver</i>
			(post-class. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium falsorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 321, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">evangelii,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the author</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res Carn. 33</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An interpreter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 17, 2, § 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. E. 6,
		11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
